ates the issue: it states each of the 12 measurement rows was entered as one observation in a two-sample Student t-test (scipy.stats.ttest_ind, equal_var=True) with n = 6 per arm and t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133.\",\"The report's Interpretation section explicitly confirms the pseudoreplication: the 12 analysed rows are the 2 nubbins measured on each of the 6 parent colonies, and the test used all 12 rows as observations, 'which is where its 10 degrees of freedom come from' — repeated measurements from the same colony entered into a row-independent procedure as if independent (a colony-level analysis would have only 4 df).\",\"The workflow code corroborates this: rates_by_regime pools all rows per regime with no per-colony aggregation before stats.ttest_ind.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column colony_id is consistent with the frozen data: six colony labels (CL01-CL06) each appear on exactly two rows, thermal_regime is constant within each colony, and both arms (ambient: CL01-CL03; heated: CL04-CL06) have three colonies contributing two nubbin rows each, matching the description of nubbins as repeated measurements of their parent colony.","The selected report demonstrates the issue: it states each of the 12 measurement rows was entered as one observation in a two-sample Student t-test (scipy.stats.ttest_ind, equal_var=True) with n = 6 per arm and t(10) = 3.0000, p = 0.0133.","The report's Interpretation section explicitly confirms the pseudoreplication: the 12 analysed rows are the 2 nubbins measured on each of the 6 parent colonies, and the test used all 12 rows as observations, 'which is where its 10 degrees of freedom come from' — repeated measurements from the same colony entered into a row-independent procedure as if independent (a colony-level analysis would have only 4 df).","The workflow code corroborates this: rates_by_regime pools all rows per regime with no per-colony aggregation before stats.ttest_ind.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":6375,"ttft_stream_ms":1945,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":18007,"uuid":"03cd16a7-68e0-4ecc-95db-13c18c455ba0"}
